xprof-rs

This project is a new implementation of two parts of other projects:
- the trace-viewer conversion pipeline of OpenXLA XProf (https://github.com/openxla/xprof)
- the profiler utilities of OpenXLA XLA/TSL (https://github.com/openxla/xla)

The TensorFlow Authors hold the copyright of both projects. Both projects use the Apache License 2.0.

The web interface that xprof-rs serves is the interface of XProf. The files in ui/ are the files of the XProf 2.23.2
Python package (Apache License 2.0, copyright The TensorFlow Authors), with these changes:
- index.html starts the bundle after Google Charts loads its packages. It keeps the Intl.NumberFormat objects that
  Number.prototype.toLocaleString makes, and it gets styles.css and zone.js only one time.
- bundle.js draws a chart one time when its data and its filters change. The memory viewer draws its charts one time.
- trace_viewer_index.js calculates the hash of a string with fewer operations. To find the slice of an event, it uses a
  binary search.
The build compresses these files, and the binary includes them. ui/materialicons.woff2 is the Material Icons font of
Google (Apache License 2.0). The JavaScript bundles include third-party libraries with their licenses, as in the XProf package.
